#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/036_flax_in_the_field/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Flax was soaked, beaten and combed for weeks before it could be spun into linen."
msgstr "El lino se remojaba, se golpeaba y se peinaba durante semanas antes de hilarlo."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/037_barley_for_the_brewer/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Barley for the Brewer"
msgstr "Cebada para el cervecero"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/037_barley_for_the_brewer/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Orm of Hallvik wants the biggest barrel of ale for the autumn feast. I need grain, five crates! "
"Bring them, and you get two crates of my ale."
msgstr ""
"Orm de Hallvik quiere el barril de cerveza más grande para la fiesta de otoño. ¡Necesito grano, "
"cinco cajas! {crew|Tráemelas|Tráemelas|Traédmelas} y {crew|te doy|te doy|os doy} dos cajas de mi "
"cerveza."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/037_barley_for_the_brewer/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Into the water with it, let it sprout... In a week, the best ale of the lakes!"
msgstr "Al agua con él, que brote... ¡En una semana, la mejor cerveza de los lagos!"

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/037_barley_for_the_brewer/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Ale was brewed from barley and water, often with herbs instead of hops."
msgstr "La cerveza se hacía con cebada y agua, a menudo con hierbas en lugar de lúpulo."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/038_a_proper_hold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "A Proper Hold"
msgstr "Una bodega de verdad"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/038_a_proper_hold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"You are real traders now: you need a real hold! Bring me eight planks from Frosttorp and two "
"crates of iron tools, and pay 20 silver. Then your hold takes two more crates."
msgstr ""
"Ya {crew|eres un comerciante de verdad|eres una comerciante de verdad|sois comerciantes de "
"verdad|sois comerciantes de verdad}: ¡{crew|necesitas|necesitas|necesitáis} una bodega de verdad! "
"{crew|Tráeme|Tráeme|Traedme} ocho tablas de Frosttorp y dos cajas de herramientas de hierro, y "
"{crew|paga|paga|pagad} 20 monedas de plata. Así en {crew|tu|tu|vuestra} bodega cabrán dos cajas "
"más."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/038_a_proper_hold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Planks of pine, split with wedges. Stack them well!"
msgstr "Tablas de pino, partidas con cuñas. ¡{crew|Apílalas|Apílalas|Apiladlas} bien!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/038_a_proper_hold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Good iron! Now my wages."
msgstr "¡Buen hierro! Ahora mi paga."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/038_a_proper_hold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Saw, plane, rivets... Look at her! Longer, wider, and room for two more crates."
msgstr ""
"Sierra, cepillo, remaches... ¡{crew|Mira|Mira|Mirad} qué barco! Más largo, más ancho, y con sitio "
"para dos cajas más."

