msgid "{count|a wheel of cheese|{count} wheels of cheese}"
msgstr ""

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/041_sigvors_cheese/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Cheese keeps the milk of the summer for the winter."
msgstr "El queso guarda la leche del verano para el invierno."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/042_a_cow_of_our_own/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "A Cow of Our Own"
msgstr "Una vaca para nosotros"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/042_a_cow_of_our_own/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"With the east meadow, we have room for a cow at last! Buy one at the horse farm in Torsgården. A "
"cow is big, but she fits in your boat like a crate, if she stands still."
msgstr ""
"Con el prado del este, ¡por fin tenemos sitio para una vaca! {crew|Compra|Compra|Comprad} una en "
"la granja de caballos de Torsgården. Una vaca es grande, pero cabe en el barco como una caja, si "
"se queda quieta."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/042_a_cow_of_our_own/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Look at her big brown eyes! She will give us milk every day. Let us call her Rosa."
msgstr ""
"¡{crew|Mira|Mira|Mirad} qué ojos tan grandes y marrones! Nos dará leche todos los días. La "
"llamaremos Rosa."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/042_a_cow_of_our_own/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Cows were the wealth of a farm: a family counted its riches in cows."
msgstr "Las vacas eran la riqueza de una granja: una familia contaba lo que tenía en vacas."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/043_pots_for_ekvik/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Pots for Ekvik"
msgstr "Vasijas para Ekvik"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/043_pots_for_ekvik/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The fish soup! We cook it for the whole village, but our big pot cracked. Bring us three crates of"
" pots from the potter, please."
msgstr ""
"¡La sopa de pescado! La hacemos para todo el pueblo, pero nuestra olla grande se ha rajado. "
"{crew|Tráenos|Tráenos|Traednos} tres cajas de vasijas de la alfarera, por favor."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/043_pots_for_ekvik/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "New pots! Tonight there is fish soup for everybody, and for you two the first bowl."
msgstr ""
"¡Vasijas nuevas! Esta noche hay sopa de pescado para todos, y el primer cuenco es para "
"{crew|ti|ti|vosotros|vosotras}."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/043_pots_for_ekvik/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The cooking pot hung over the fire on a chain, and the soup simmered all day."
msgstr "La olla colgaba de una cadena sobre el fuego, y la sopa hervía a fuego lento todo el día."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/044_ragnas_broken_oar/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Ragna's Broken Oar"
msgstr "El remo roto de Ragna"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/044_ragnas_broken_oar/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Ragna rowed out at dawn and is not back! I fear her oar broke. Find her on the lakes, then come "
"back and fetch the spare oar for her."
msgstr ""
"¡Ragna salió a remar al amanecer y no ha vuelto! Me temo que se le ha roto el remo. "
"{crew|Búscala|Búscala|Buscadla} en los lagos, y luego {crew|vuelve|vuelve|volved} a por el remo de"
" repuesto para ella."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/044_ragnas_broken_oar/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Hello! Yes, my oar broke, and I drift with one. Tell Tor to give you the spare one!"
msgstr ""
"¡Hola! Sí, se me rompió el remo, y voy a la deriva con uno solo. ¡{crew|Dile|Dile|Decidle} a Tor "
"que {crew|te dé|te dé|os dé} el de repuesto!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/044_ragnas_broken_oar/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "She is well? Thank the gods. Here is the oar: bring it to her!"
msgstr ""
"¿Está bien? Gracias a los dioses. Aquí está el remo: ¡{crew|llévaselo|llévaselo|llevádselo}!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/044_ragnas_broken_oar/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "My oar! Now I can row again. Here, take some fish: the freshest on the lakes."
msgstr ""
"¡Mi remo! Ya puedo volver a remar. {crew|Toma|Toma|Tomad}, un poco de pescado: el más fresco de "
"los lagos."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/044_ragnas_broken_oar/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Every viking boat carried spare oars: a broken oar was common."
msgstr "Todos los barcos vikingos llevaban remos de repuesto: romper un remo era algo corriente."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/045_torches_for_the_dark/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Torches for the Dark"
msgstr "Antorchas para la noche"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/045_torches_for_the_dark/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The nights grow long. The guests of the autumn feast need light: bring me tar for torches, two "
"pots from Ekvik, and two crates of flax for the wicks."
msgstr ""
"Las noches se hacen largas. Los invitados de la fiesta de otoño necesitan luz: "
"{crew|tráeme|tráeme|traedme} brea para antorchas, dos ollas de Ekvik, y dos cajas de lino para las"
" mechas."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/045_torches_for_the_dark/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Tar for torches? They burn bright and long."
msgstr "¿Brea para antorchas? Arden mucho rato y con mucha luz."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/045_torches_for_the_dark/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Tar and flax: now my torches will light up the whole bay!"
msgstr "Brea y lino: ¡ahora mis antorchas iluminarán toda la bahía!"

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/045_torches_for_the_dark/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Viking torches were sticks wrapped in flax or cloth, soaked in tar or fat."
msgstr "Las antorchas vikingas eran palos envueltos en lino o tela, empapados en brea o grasa."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/046_the_autumn_feast/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Autumn Feast"
msgstr "La fiesta de otoño"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/046_the_autumn_feast/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The autumn feast is tomorrow! Knut's ale is ready, five barrels. Bring them from Lindtorp, and "
"bring three crates of fish for the soup too."
msgstr ""
"¡La fiesta de otoño es mañana! La cerveza de Knut está lista, cinco barriles. "
"{crew|Tráelos|Tráelos|Traedlos} de Lindtorp, y {crew|trae|trae|traed} también tres cajas de "
"pescado para la sopa."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/046_the_autumn_feast/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The ale! Now the fish."
msgstr "¡La cerveza! Ahora el pescado."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/046_the_autumn_feast/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The biggest batch I ever brewed! Five barrels for Orm."
msgstr "¡La mayor tanda que he hecho nunca! Cinco barriles para Orm."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/046_the_autumn_feast/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Ale, soup, torches, Sten's flute and Hrafn's knives! Everybody is here. Dance with us!"
msgstr ""
"¡Cerveza, sopa, antorchas, la flauta de Sten y los cuchillos de Hrafn! Está todo el mundo. "
"¡{crew|Baila|Baila|Bailad} con nosotros!"

