#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/049_the_runestone/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Runestones were raised for loved ones, and painted in bright colours."
msgstr "Las piedras rúnicas se levantaban por los seres queridos, y se pintaban de colores vivos."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/050_the_first_snow/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The First Snow"
msgstr "La primera nevada"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/050_the_first_snow/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Snowflakes! Winter is near. Our store needs feed for the animals: six crates of hay and four of "
"grain. Your hold takes eight: think how to row it!"
msgstr ""
"¡Copos de nieve! Se acerca el invierno. Nuestro almacén necesita comida para los animales: seis "
"cajas de heno y cuatro de grano. En {crew|tu|tu|vuestra} bodega caben ocho: "
"¡{crew|piensa|piensa|pensad} cómo llevarlo!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/050_the_first_snow/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Hay for the sheep, the goats and Rosa. Now the grain."
msgstr "Heno para las ovejas, las cabras y Rosa. Ahora el grano."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/050_the_first_snow/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The store is full! Let the snow come. Come in, the soup is hot."
msgstr ""
"¡El almacén está lleno! Que venga la nieve. {crew|Entra|Entra|Entrad}, la sopa está caliente."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/050_the_first_snow/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "In winter, the animals stayed in the barn for months and ate the hay of the summer."
msgstr "En invierno, los animales se quedaban meses en el establo y comían el heno del verano."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/051_the_ice_breaks/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Ice Breaks"
msgstr "Se rompe el hielo"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/051_the_ice_breaks/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Hear that crack? The ice breaks: spring is here again! Row out and hail two boats: ask how "
"everybody got through the winter."
msgstr ""
"¿{crew|Oyes|Oyes|Oís} ese crujido? El hielo se rompe: ¡vuelve la primavera! {crew|Sal|Sal|Salid} a"
" remar y {crew|saluda|saluda|saludad} a dos barcos: {crew|pregunta|pregunta|preguntad} cómo han "
"pasado todos el invierno."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/051_the_ice_breaks/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Everybody is well! But Tova has asked for you all winter. Row to Laxön!"
msgstr ""
"¡Todos estamos bien! Pero Tova ha preguntado por {crew|ti|ti|vosotros|vosotras} todo el invierno. "
"¡{crew|Rema|Rema|Remad} hasta Laxön!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/051_the_ice_breaks/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "A long winter! But the herring kept, thanks to your salt."
msgstr "¡Qué invierno tan largo! Pero los arenques aguantaron, gracias a {crew|tu|tu|vuestra} sal."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/051_the_ice_breaks/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"There you are! Spring is when the animals need us most. Will you be my apprentices, and learn to "
"heal?"
msgstr ""
"¡Ahí {crew|estás|estás|estáis}! En primavera es cuando los animales más nos necesitan. "
"¿{crew|Quieres ser mi aprendiz|Quieres ser mi aprendiz|Queréis ser mis aprendices} y aprender a "
"curar?"

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/051_the_ice_breaks/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "When the ice broke in spring, the boats came out, and with them the news."
msgstr "Cuando el hielo se rompía en primavera, salían los barcos, y con ellos las noticias."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/052_the_coughing_horse/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Coughing Horse"
msgstr "El caballo que tose"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/052_the_coughing_horse/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Your first case as healers: Ragnfrid's old horse Bror coughs. Take him this syrup of thyme and "
"honey, then come back to me after a night, to hear how he is."
msgstr ""
"{crew|Tu|Tu|Vuestro} primer caso de {crew|curandero|curandera|curanderos|curanderas}: Bror, el "
"caballo viejo de Ragnfrid, tose. {crew|Llévale|Llévale|Llevadle} este jarabe de tomillo y miel, y "
"{crew|vuelve|vuelve|volved} a verme después de una noche, para saber cómo está."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/052_the_coughing_horse/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Thyme and honey? Bror loves it. He licks the spoon!"
msgstr "¿Tomillo y miel? A Bror le encanta. ¡Lame la cuchara!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/052_the_coughing_horse/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "He slept the whole night and coughs no more. Tell Tova: her apprentices are good!"
msgstr ""
"Ha dormido toda la noche y ya no tose. {crew|Dile|Dile|Decidle} a Tova: ¡{crew|su aprendiz es "
"bueno|su aprendiz es buena|sus aprendices son buenos|sus aprendices son buenas}!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/052_the_coughing_horse/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Well done! You listened, you waited, you looked. That is healing."
msgstr ""
"¡Muy bien! {crew|Has escuchado, has esperado, has mirado|Has escuchado, has esperado, has "
"mirado|Habéis escuchado, habéis esperado, habéis mirado}. Eso es curar."

#. a thing of a task, under its crate: at most 10 letters
#: data/missions/052_the_coughing_horse/mission.json
#, fuzzy
