msgid "Twelve crates! Nobody in the north goes hungry this winter. The whole valley thanks you."
msgstr ""
"¡Doce cajas! Nadie en el norte pasará hambre este invierno. Todo el valle {crew|te|te|os} da las "
"gracias."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/083_grain_for_the_north/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "When the harvest failed, the farms helped each other: next year, it might be them."
msgstr "Cuando la cosecha salía mal, las granjas se ayudaban: al año siguiente podían ser ellas."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/084_the_wool_fair/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Wool Fair"
msgstr "La feria de la lana"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/084_the_wool_fair/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The wool fair! Traders come from the Long Lake to buy. Bring me eight crates of wool, the more the"
" better, and the fair is a success."
msgstr ""
"¡La feria de la lana! Vienen comerciantes del Lago Largo a comprar. {crew|Tráeme|Tráeme|Traedme} "
"ocho cajas de lana, cuantas más mejor, y la feria será un éxito."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/084_the_wool_fair/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Eight crates! The traders from the Long Lake ask: who are these girls? I say: the best traders of "
"the Home Lakes."
msgstr ""
"¡Ocho cajas! Los comerciantes del Lago Largo preguntan: ¿{crew|quién es este chico|quién es esta "
"chica|quiénes son estos chicos|quiénes son estas chicas}? Yo digo: {crew|el mejor comerciante|la "
"mejor comerciante|los mejores comerciantes|las mejores comerciantes} de los Lagos de Casa."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/084_the_wool_fair/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Wool was so important that some sagas tell of whole ships full of it."
msgstr "La lana era tan importante que algunas sagas hablan de barcos enteros llenos de ella."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/085_the_goats_on_the_island/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Goats on the Island"
msgstr "Las cabras de la isla"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/085_the_goats_on_the_island/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"My four goats swam to Bergö! They eat Dagny's flowers, and she is cross. Bring them back before "
"they eat her kiln too!"
msgstr ""
"¡Mis cuatro cabras se han ido nadando a Bergö! Se comen las flores de Dagny, y ella está enfadada."
" ¡{crew|Tráelas|Tráelas|Traedlas} antes de que se coman también su horno!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/085_the_goats_on_the_island/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "My naughty goats! Tomorrow I build a higher fence. Here, my best cheese."
msgstr ""
"¡Mis cabras traviesas! Mañana hago una valla más alta. {crew|Toma|Toma|Tomad}, mi mejor queso."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/085_the_goats_on_the_island/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Take them, take them! They ate my flowers and a basket and a shoe!"
msgstr ""
"¡{crew|Llévatelas, llévatelas|Llévatelas, llévatelas|Lleváoslas, lleváoslas}! ¡Se han comido mis "
"flores, una cesta y un zapato!"

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/085_the_goats_on_the_island/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Goats are good swimmers when they must be, and they eat nearly anything."
msgstr "Las cabras nadan bien cuando hace falta, y comen casi de todo."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/086_news_for_everybody/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "News for Everybody"
msgstr "Noticias para todos"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/086_news_for_everybody/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Big news: a ship from the Long Lake will come, and the way between the lakes opens! Tell the "
"smith, the fishers of Stormvik and Orm in Hallvik. I tell the rest."
msgstr ""
"Gran noticia: vendrá un barco del Lago Largo, ¡y se abre el camino entre los lagos! "
"{crew|Avisa|Avisa|Avisad} al herrero, a los pescadores de Stormvik y a Orm, en Hallvik. Yo aviso a"
" los demás."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/086_news_for_everybody/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "A ship from the Long Lake? They will want my iron!"
msgstr "¿Un barco del Lago Largo? ¡Querrán mi hierro!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/086_news_for_everybody/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "New lakes, new fish! Thank you for telling us."
msgstr "¡Lagos nuevos, peces nuevos! Gracias por avisarnos."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/086_news_for_everybody/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Guests from far away! I must brew more. Thank you, girls!"
msgstr ""
"¡Invitados de muy lejos! Tengo que hacer más cerveza. ¡Gracias, {crew|chico|chica|chicos|chicas}!"

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/086_news_for_everybody/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The lakes of the north were joined by rivers and portages, where boats were dragged over land."
msgstr ""
"Los lagos del norte estaban unidos por ríos y pasos donde los barcos se arrastraban por tierra."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/087_a_cow_for_grim/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "A Cow for Grim"
msgstr "Una vaca para Grim"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/087_a_cow_for_grim/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"I am old, and I would like fresh milk every morning. Bring me a cow from the horse farm. The swans"
" will be jealous!"
msgstr ""
"Soy viejo, y me gustaría tener leche fresca cada mañana. {crew|Tráeme|Tráeme|Traedme} una vaca de "
"la granja de caballos. ¡Los cisnes tendrán celos!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/087_a_cow_for_grim/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"A cow! I call her Swan, ha. Here, for your trouble, and for all the years you visited an old man."
msgstr ""
"¡Una vaca! La llamaré Cisne, ja. {crew|Toma|Toma|Tomad}, por la molestia, y por todos los años que"
" {crew|has visitado|has visitado|habéis visitado} a un viejo."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/087_a_cow_for_grim/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "A good cow gave milk for ten years or more, and was part of the family."
msgstr "Una buena vaca daba leche diez años o más, y era parte de la familia."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/088_flowers_on_the_hill/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Flowers on the Hill"
msgstr "Flores en la colina"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/088_flowers_on_the_hill/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Plant flowers on the sunny hill! When they bloom, bring three crates to Gudrun's inn: she wants "
"the inn to smell like summer."
msgstr ""
"¡{crew|Siembra|Siembra|Sembrad} flores en la colina soleada! Cuando florezcan, "
"{crew|lleva|lleva|llevad} tres cajas a la posada de Gudrun: quiere que la posada huela a verano."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/088_flowers_on_the_hill/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Flower seeds in the earth. In two days, they bloom."
msgstr "Semillas de flores en la tierra. En dos días, florecerán."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/088_flowers_on_the_hill/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Flowers on every table! The guests smile. Here is your silver, and a cup of milk for each of you."
msgstr ""
"¡Flores en todas las mesas! Los invitados sonríen. Aquí {crew|tienes tu|tienes tu|tenéis vuestra} "
"plata, y un vaso de leche {crew|para ti|para ti|para cada uno|para cada una}."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/088_flowers_on_the_hill/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Vikings wove flowers into wreaths and crowns for feasts and weddings."
msgstr "Los vikingos trenzaban flores en coronas y guirnaldas para fiestas y bodas."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/089_the_pottery_market/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Pottery Market"
msgstr "El mercado de vasijas"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/089_the_pottery_market/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The new kiln makes so many pots! Bring ten crates to the market in Kråkhamn. Ten crates: only your"
" big boat can do it."
msgstr ""
"¡El horno nuevo hace muchísimas vasijas! {crew|Lleva|Lleva|Llevad} diez cajas al mercado de "
"Kråkhamn. Diez cajas: solo {crew|tu|tu|vuestro} barco grande puede hacerlo."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/089_the_pottery_market/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Ten crates of Dagny's pots, and not one broken! The best rowing of the lakes."
msgstr "¡Diez cajas de vasijas de Dagny, y ni una rota! Nadie rema mejor en los lagos."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/089_the_pottery_market/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Pack them in straw: pots do not like to bump!"
msgstr "{crew|Mételas|Mételas|Metedlas} en paja: ¡a las vasijas no les gustan los golpes!"

#. a thing of a task, under its crate: at most 10 letters
#: data/missions/089_the_pottery_market/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Pots"
