#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/090_gudruns_ring/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Vikings sometimes gave silver to the lakes on purpose, as gifts to the gods."
msgstr "A veces los vikingos echaban plata a los lagos a propósito, como regalo a los dioses."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/091_the_edge_of_the_forest/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Edge of the Forest"
msgstr "El borde del bosque"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/091_the_edge_of_the_forest/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Kol and Ingrid want sheep for their new home. Bring them two sheep, and I give you the strip of "
"land by the forest, next to your farm. A fair trade!"
msgstr ""
"Kol e Ingrid quieren ovejas para su casa nueva. {crew|Llévales|Llévales|Llevadles} dos ovejas, y "
"{crew|te doy|te doy|os doy} la franja de tierra junto al bosque, al lado de {crew|tu|tu|vuestra} "
"granja. ¡Un trato justo!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/091_the_edge_of_the_forest/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Two sheep for the young ones! Ingrid already knits. The forest edge is yours: good wood and two "
"fields."
msgstr ""
"¡Dos ovejas para los jóvenes! Ingrid ya teje. El borde del bosque es {crew|tuyo|tuyo|vuestro}: "
"buena madera y dos campos."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/091_the_edge_of_the_forest/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Land was traded for animals, silver or work: there were no banks."
msgstr "La tierra se cambiaba por animales, plata o trabajo: no había bancos."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/092_the_longhouse_grows/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Longhouse Grows"
msgstr "La casa larga crece"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/092_the_longhouse_grows/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"With so many animals and friends, our house is too small! Bring twelve logs from Frosttorp, two "
"crates of tools and two pots of tar, and we make it longer."
msgstr ""
"Con tantos animales y amigos, ¡nuestra casa se ha quedado pequeña! {crew|Trae|Trae|Traed} doce "
"troncos de Frosttorp, dos cajas de herramientas y dos ollas de brea, y la alargaremos."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/092_the_longhouse_grows/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Twelve logs! Fill that big hold of yours."
msgstr "¡Doce troncos! {crew|Llena|Llena|Llenad} bien esa bodega tan grande."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/092_the_longhouse_grows/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Axes and nails. Now the tar for the roof."
msgstr "Hachas y clavos. Ahora la brea para el tejado."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/092_the_longhouse_grows/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Hammering all night with the neighbours... Our longhouse is twice as long! Room for a feast."
msgstr ""
"Martillazos toda la noche con los vecinos... ¡Nuestra casa larga es el doble de larga! Hay sitio "
"para una fiesta."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/092_the_longhouse_grows/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "A longhouse could be made longer by adding a piece at the end, like a train."
msgstr "Una casa larga se podía alargar añadiendo un trozo al final, como un tren."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/093_the_green_valley/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Green Valley"
msgstr "El valle verde"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/093_the_green_valley/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"You helped my valley all year. The green valley behind your farm has no owner: bring me two crates"
" of cloth and two of honey for the gods' feast, and it is yours."
msgstr ""
"{crew|Has ayudado|Has ayudado|Habéis ayudado} a mi valle todo el año. El valle verde detrás de "
"{crew|tu|tu|vuestra} granja no tiene dueño: {crew|tráeme|tráeme|traedme} dos cajas de tela y dos "
"de miel para la fiesta de los dioses, y será {crew|tuyo|tuyo|vuestro}."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/093_the_green_valley/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Cloth for the hall. Now the honey."
msgstr "Tela para la sala. Ahora la miel."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/093_the_green_valley/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Father says it at the Thing, in front of everybody: the green valley belongs to Ylva and Sigrid!"
msgstr "Mi padre lo dice en el Thing, delante de todos: ¡el valle verde es de Ylva y Sigrid!"

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/093_the_green_valley/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "At the Thing, the meeting of the free people, land and laws were decided."
msgstr "En el Thing, la asamblea de la gente libre, se decidían las tierras y las leyes."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/094_bees_for_the_valley/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bees for the Valley"
msgstr "Abejas para el valle"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/094_bees_for_the_valley/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The valley is full of clover and heather. Bees would love it! Have three beehives on the farm, and"
" we will have honey all year."
msgstr ""
"El valle está lleno de trébol y brezo. ¡A las abejas les encantaría! {crew|Ten|Ten|Tened} tres "
"colmenas en la granja, y tendremos miel todo el año."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/094_bees_for_the_valley/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Hum, hum, hum! Three hives in the valley. Honey for us, and for mead."
msgstr "¡Zum, zum, zum! Tres colmenas en el valle. Miel para nosotros, y para hidromiel."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/094_bees_for_the_valley/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Heather honey is dark and strong; clover honey is light and mild."
msgstr "La miel de brezo es oscura y fuerte; la de trébol es clara y suave."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/095_apples_for_the_market/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Apples for the Market"
msgstr "Manzanas para el mercado"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/095_apples_for_the_market/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Thanks to the bees, my trees are full of apples! Twelve baskets for the market in Kråkhamn. Only "
"your boat can take them all at once."
msgstr ""
"Gracias a las abejas, ¡mis árboles están llenos de manzanas! Doce cestas para el mercado de "
"Kråkhamn. Solo {crew|tu|tu|vuestro} barco puede llevarlas todas a la vez."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/095_apples_for_the_market/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Twelve baskets of apples! The whole market smells of autumn."
msgstr "¡Doce cestas de manzanas! Todo el mercado huele a otoño."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/095_apples_for_the_market/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Red and green and yellow. Take one for the trip!"
msgstr "Rojas, verdes y amarillas. ¡{crew|Coge|Coge|Coged} una para el viaje!"

#. a thing of a task, under its crate: at most 10 letters
#: data/missions/095_apples_for_the_market/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Apples"
msgstr "Manzanas"

